<title>DUBAI: Egyptian airliner in forced landing, all safe.</title>
<headline>Egyptian airliner in forced landing, all safe.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>An aircraft of Egyptian national carrier EgyptAir made a forced landing in the Saudi capital Riyadh on Monday night due to a technical problem during its flight from Kuwait to Cairo, airline sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>All 68 passengers, mostly Egyptians, and crew were safe and had been taken to a hotel in Riyadh, the sources said.</p>
<p>The passengers were expected to fly to Cairo on Tuesday on board another EgyptAir plane.</p>
<p>The cause of the technical problem was not immediately known, the sources said.</p>
</text>
